{
  "title": "Scholarship Application Summary",
  "subtitle": "Overview of applicant demographics, status, and geographic distribution",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Applicants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM scholarship_applicants",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Approved Count",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM scholarship_applicants WHERE \"Status\" = 'Approved'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Marks %",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Marks %\") AS avg_marks FROM scholarship_applicants",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applicants by Status",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Status\", COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM scholarship_applicants GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Status",
      "y": [
        "cnt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applicants by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM scholarship_applicants GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "District",
      "y": [
        "cnt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 5 Districts by Volume",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS total_applicants, AVG(\"Marks %\") AS avg_marks, AVG(\"Family Income\") AS avg_income FROM scholarship_applicants GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The board has received a total of {{p1}} scholarship applications. Of these, {{p2}} have been approved, indicating a significant portion of the pipeline is moving forward. The average academic performance across all applicants is {{p3}}%.\n\nGeographically, the applications are distributed across various districts, with the highest volume coming from the leading district in the bar chart. Status-wise, the majority of applicants fall into the 'Approved' or 'Pending' categories, as shown in the status breakdown.\n\nThe table above provides a detailed view of the top 5 districts by application volume, including their average marks and family income, allowing for a quick assessment of regional trends and applicant quality."
}

{
  "title": "Fitness Programme Impact Summary",
  "subtitle": "Comparing baseline and endline physical metrics to assess programme effectiveness",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Children Tracked",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM baseline",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Height Gain (cm)",
      "sql": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(end.\"Height cm\" - base.\"Height cm\"), 1) AS n FROM baseline base JOIN endline end ON base.\"Child ID\" = end.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "cm"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(end.\"Sit ups\" - base.\"Sit ups\"), 1) AS n FROM baseline base JOIN endline end ON base.\"Child ID\" = end.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Improvement (sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(base.\"Shuttle run sec\" - end.\"Shuttle run sec\"), 1) AS n FROM baseline base JOIN endline end ON base.\"Child ID\" = end.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "sec"
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Physical Metrics by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT end.\"Location\", ROUND(AVG(end.\"Height cm\" - base.\"Height cm\"), 1) AS height_gain, ROUND(AVG(end.\"Sit ups\" - base.\"Sit ups\"), 1) AS situp_gain FROM baseline base JOIN endline end ON base.\"Child ID\" = end.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "Location",
      "y": ["height_gain", "situp_gain"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Coach Performance Summary",
      "sql": "SELECT base.\"Coach\", COUNT(DISTINCT base.\"Child ID\") AS children, ROUND(AVG(end.\"Sit ups\" - base.\"Sit ups\"), 1) AS avg_situp_gain, ROUND(AVG(base.\"Shuttle run sec\" - end.\"Shuttle run sec\"), 1) AS avg_shuttle_improvement FROM baseline base JOIN endline end ON base.\"Child ID\" = end.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 3 DESC LIMIT 10",
      "unit": ""
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The programme successfully tracked {{p1}} children, providing a robust dataset to evaluate physical development. On average, participants showed positive growth in key fitness indicators. The average height gain was {{p2}}, demonstrating consistent physical development over the programme duration. In terms of strength and endurance, the average improvement in sit-ups was {{p3}}, while the average improvement in shuttle run time was {{p4}}, indicating better agility and speed. Regional variations are visible in {{p5}}, where certain locations showed higher gains in height and sit-ups, suggesting localized effectiveness or demographic differences. Finally, {{p6}} highlights the top-performing coaches based on the average improvement in sit-ups and shuttle run times, offering insights into which coaching styles or efforts correlate with the best physical outcomes for the children."
}

{
  "title": "Fitness Programme Results",
  "subtitle": "Summary of participant growth and performance metrics for donor review",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Participants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Child ID\") AS n FROM baseline",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Height Gain (cm)",
      "sql": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(b.\"Height cm\" - e.\"Height cm\"), 1) AS n FROM baseline AS b JOIN endline AS e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": "cm"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-up Gain",
      "sql": "SELECT ROUND(AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\"), 1) AS n FROM baseline AS b JOIN endline AS e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Height Gain by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT e.\"Location\", ROUND(AVG(e.\"Height cm\" - b.\"Height cm\"), 1) AS avg_height_gain FROM baseline AS b JOIN endline AS e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "Location",
      "y": ["avg_height_gain"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 10 Coaches by Sit-up Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT e.\"Coach\", COUNT(DISTINCT e.\"Child ID\") AS children, ROUND(AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\"), 1) AS avg_situp_gain FROM baseline AS b JOIN endline AS e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 3 DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The programme engaged {{p1}} children across multiple locations. On average, participants showed significant physical improvement, with an average height gain of {{p2}} cm and an average increase of {{p3}} sit-ups. Regional performance varied, with the top location achieving an average height gain of {{p4.avg_height_gain}}. Coaching effectiveness was also measured, with the top-performing coach's team showing an average sit-up gain of {{p5.avg_situp_gain}}."
}

{
  "title": "Gender Performance Gap Analysis",
  "subtitle": "Comparing baseline to endline improvements in physical fitness metrics by gender",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Children Tracked",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM baseline UNION SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM endline) t",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement (Boys)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS n FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Male'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement (Girls)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS n FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Female'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Sit-ups Improvement by Gender",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Gender\", AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Gender",
      "y": ["improvement"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Shuttle Run Improvement by Gender (Sec)",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Gender\", AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 ASC",
      "x": "Gender",
      "y": ["improvement"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Detailed Metrics by Gender",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Gender\", COUNT(*) AS n, AVG(b.\"Sit ups\") AS baseline_situps, AVG(e.\"Sit ups\") AS endline_situps, AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS baseline_shuttle, AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS endline_shuttle FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "To determine if girls and boys are improving equally, we compare the delta between baseline and endline measurements for key physical indicators. The total cohort size is {{p1}} children.\n\nIn terms of muscular endurance (Sit-ups), boys showed an average improvement of {{p2}} repetitions, while girls improved by {{p3}} repetitions. This suggests a disparity in strength gains if the values differ significantly.\n\nFor cardiovascular agility (Shuttle Run), lower times are better. The bar chart {{p5}} shows the change in seconds. A negative value indicates improvement (faster time). Comparing the bars in {{p4}} and {{p5}} reveals which gender is gaining more in each domain.\n\nThe table {{p6}} provides the raw averages. If the gap between baseline and endline is wider for one gender in both metrics, that group is improving more rapidly. If one improves in speed but the other in strength, the improvement is complementary rather than equal."
}

{
  "title": "SHG Loan Repayment & Purpose Analysis",
  "subtitle": "Overview of loan disbursements, repayment status distribution, and purpose breakdown across blocks.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Loans Disbursed",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"shg_loan_register\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Loan Amount (Rs)",
      "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\") AS total_amount FROM \"shg_loan_register\"",
      "unit": "Rs"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "pie",
      "title": "Repayment Status Distribution",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Repayment Status\", COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM \"shg_loan_register\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Repayment Status",
      "y": ["cnt"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Loan Amount by Purpose",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Purpose\", AVG(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\") AS avg_amount FROM \"shg_loan_register\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Purpose",
      "y": ["avg_amount"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Blocks by Overdue Loans",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Block\", COUNT(*) AS overdue_count, SUM(\"Loan Amount (Rs)\") AS overdue_amount FROM \"shg_loan_register\" WHERE \"Repayment Status\" = 'Overdue' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The SHG program has disbursed {{p1}} loans totaling {{p2}}. The majority of these loans are in good standing, with only a fraction marked as overdue as shown in the repayment status pie chart. When analyzing loan purposes, {{p4}} indicates which category receives the highest average funding. For risk management, it is critical to monitor the top blocks listed in the table below, where overdue concentrations are highest."
}
